    summary: "SonicWall針對已退役的集中管理平臺GMS（Global Management System）發布安全性更新，修補包含遠端執行任意程式碼在內的6個漏洞。受影響版本為GMS Virtual Appliance與Windows版9.5.1以前版本。其中最嚴重的漏洞為CVE-2026-66147，CVSS評分達9.4分，允許攻擊者透過特製請求在未經驗證下遠端執行任意程式碼；另一漏洞CVE-2026-66145評分達9.1分，可能導致遠端執行程式碼、敏感資料讀取及Zipslip任意檔案寫入。目前尚無遭實際利用之證據，官方建議用戶升級至9.5.2以上版本。",
    tags: ["SonicWall", "GMS", "CVE-2026-66147", "CVE-2026-66145", "遠端程式碼執行", "資安漏洞"],
    title_en: "SonicWall Patches Six Vulnerabilities in Retired Global Management System (GMS), Including Critical Remote Code Execution Flaw",
    summary_en: "SonicWall has released a security update for its retired Global Management System (GMS), patching six vulnerabilities, including a remote arbitrary code execution flaw. Affected versions include GMS Virtual Appliance and Windows versions 9.5.1 and earlier. The most severe vulnerability is CVE-2026-66147, which scores 9.4 on CVSS and allows an attacker to remotely execute arbitrary code without authentication via a specially crafted request. Another vulnerability, CVE-2026-66145, scores 9.1 and could lead to remote code execution, sensitive data reading, and Zipslip arbitrary file write. Currently, there is no evidence of active exploitation, and the vendor recommends that users upgrade to version 9.5.2 or later.",
