    summary_en: "According to supply chain sources, Apple's next-generation A20 Pro chip is slated for release in September, powering the iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone Ultra. This chip is rumored to be Apple's first to utilize TSMC's 2nm process and is also expected to adopt the new Wafer-Level Multi-Chip Module (WMCM) packaging technology. Compared to the previous A19 Pro, the A20 Pro is projected to deliver an 18% performance boost and a 30% power efficiency improvement. These enhancements are expected to result in longer battery life while providing stronger computing performance. Combined with system optimizations in iOS 27, the iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone Ultra are anticipated to see significant performance upgrades.",
