    summary_en: "Google announced the hiring of Jacob Bank as the Vice President of Product for Chrome. Bank previously worked at Google for six years, where he was responsible for integrating his own creation, the Timeful smart calendar assistant, and participated in the development of products like Google Calendar and Gmail, adding features such as Smart Reply and Smart Compose, and utilizing AI to enhance anti-malware and anti-phishing protection. He also founded the workflow automation platform Relay.app, and several former employees from that platform joined the Chrome team. Bank stated that Chrome has become the user's primary productivity workspace and anticipates integrating more ambitious AI features, allowing users to collaborate directly with AI agents within the browser. Google currently offers Gemini within Chrome, an assistant with browser-specific capabilities that can integrate automatically with Spark, aiming to enable users to complete complex workflows within a single interface.",
